  "description": "E37 arm e37b — concept memory + reasoner, 30M testbed. New against e37a_s30: a 2-layer, width-512 reasoner over the concepts, looped twice; its update is added to each concept's mean value and to its member tokens' values. Protocol: 1.5B FineWeb-Edu tokens in rows of 4,096, then a 0.2B LongDocs-lite decay in rows of 16,384, 64 rows per step (E33p stage 1). Built 2026-11-07; status done (as of 2026-11-08). Done 8 Nov 01:11 UTC: 99.8 % at 16k, 89 % at 64k; −0.2 points vs e37a at 16k, so the reasoner is shelved for stage B (K2). Spec: docs/experiments_specs/ahead/E37_concept_memory.md. Source: origin/arch-10m @ 95ee75d. Not a builder field: Grouping, statistics and the choice have no weights (0-parameter custom cells); the summaries are the concepts' mean key and value (a notes cell with no projections); the block window and opened tokens are drawn as a 1,280-key window. The summaries' length scale past the training length (concept_sum_len, arch-10m e9b37d2, 8 Nov) is an eval switch with no weights, off in training. The reasoner's attention over earlier blocks' concepts is counted for its own block only. Parameters: 75,323,092 in total, 32,882,004 without the word tables (input embedding 13,493,056 + output layer 28,948,032); exact against the trainer's own count (evaluation/text_checks.count_params on scripts/run_e33n.py --arm e37b --size s30 (FFN 1472 from fit())). The testbed is called “30M” after the notebook arms' 30.2M without word tables (Kaplan et al.'s convention).",
